{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brusque-tippable-sunbittern","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nClosing bug 94a3-1323-3497-4f59 failed twice on the completion-verification gate, at\n`REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS` of both 480 (the default) and 1200. Both runs died the same way:\n\n    step 'decide@then/verify' failed: agent exceeded its step budget\n    (max_iterations=480; ~1 model request per tool call)\n\nThe telemetry shows this is a LOOP, not an under-sized budget. From the 480-step run:\n\n    requests=240 tool_calls=260 distinct=120 max_consecutive_repeat=131\n    top_repeats=[{'signature': 'search_files:831f8022', 'count': 132}, ...]\n\n131 CONSECUTIVE repeats of one identical `search_files` call, out of 260 total tool calls —\nmore than half the budget spent re-issuing a single byte-identical query. Raising the budget\nto 1200 simply let it loop longer and fail again, which is the diagnostic: a budget increase\ncannot fix a non-progressing loop.\n\nThe user-visible cost is that a legitimately complete ticket cannot be closed through the\ngate. The only escape the error names is `--force-close`, which discards the completion\nattestation entirely — so an infrastructure loop silently pushes authors toward bypassing a\nsafety gate, which is exactly the wrong lesson.\n\n## Approach\n\nShort-circuit non-progressing repetition in the agentic runner: track a signature of each tool\ncall (the runner already computes one — the `search_files:831f8022` form appears in the\nexisting step-budget telemetry) and, when the same signature repeats consecutively beyond a\nsmall threshold, stop the agent and return a distinct, actionable outcome rather than letting\nit burn to the step ceiling.\n\nTwo parts:\n\n1. Detect and stop. The consecutive-repeat counter already exists for telemetry\n   (`max_consecutive_repeat`); promote it to a control signal with a configurable threshold\n   (default small, e.g. 5 — well above legitimate retry-with-backoff, far below 131).\n2. Report it distinctly. A loop must NOT surface as \"exceeded its step budget ... Raise\n   REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS\", because that advice is wrong for a loop and the author will follow it\n   and lose another ten minutes. It needs its own message naming the repeated call and saying\n   that raising the budget will not help.\n\nWhy this rather than just raising the default budget: the observed failure is unbounded\nrepetition, so no finite ceiling fixes it — it only changes how long the author waits before\nthe same error. Detecting non-progress is the smallest change that turns an infinite class of\nfailure into a bounded, correctly-explained one.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/` — the agentic runner that enforces `max_iterations` and already records\n  `max_consecutive_repeat` / `top_repeats` in its step-budget telemetry; add the threshold\n  check and the distinct outcome there.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` — the close-gate message that currently renders the\n  step-budget remedy; render the loop outcome's own remedy when that is the cause.\n- `tests/unit/` — the tests below.\n- `docs/llm-framework.md` — document the loop guard and its threshold.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a fake runner that returns the same tool-call signature repeatedly is stopped at\n  the threshold, not at `max_iterations`.\n- Edge: a runner that repeats a signature fewer times than the threshold, interleaved with\n  progress, runs to completion and is NOT stopped.\n- Failure path: the resulting close-gate error names the repeated call and does not advise\n  raising `REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An agentic step whose tool-call signature repeats consecutively beyond the threshold is\n      stopped at that point; verified by a test asserting the run ends after threshold+1 calls\n      rather than after `max_iterations`.\n- [ ] A run that repeats a signature below the threshold, with progress in between, still\n      completes normally; verified by a test.\n- [ ] The loop outcome is reported distinctly from a genuine budget exhaustion and does NOT\n      advise raising `REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS`; verified by a test asserting the message contains\n      the repeated call's name and not that advice.\n- [ ] The threshold is configurable and defaults to a value below 10; verified by a test\n      reading the default.\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` documents the loop guard; verified by a grep.\n\n## Provenance\n\nReproduced twice on 94a3-1323-3497-4f59 while closing it after its change merged\n(Gerrit 1434). The ticket could not be closed through the gate and `--force-close` was\ndeliberately NOT used.\n","id":"46a2-9c1a-d855-4706","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion verifier burns its whole step budget re-issuing one identical tool call"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785954343077744001,"uuid":"283f3884-8075-4a5f-a2aa-170328120951"}